{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff --check; git diff -- site/robots.txt; cat ANSWER.md; python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrules=[]\nfor line in Path('site/robots.txt').read_text().splitlines():\n    if line.startswith(('Allow:', 'Disallow:')):\n        kind, path=line.split(': ',1)\n        rules.append((kind,path))\nfor path in ['/v1/notes','/v1/notes/drip-line-pressure','/v1/notes/drip-line-pressure/reactions','/v1/me','/v1/auth/token','/admin/']:\n    matches=[(len(rule.replace('*','')), kind,rule) for kind,rule in rules if (path.startswith(rule) if '*' not in rule else path.startswith(rule.split('*')[0]) and path.endswith(rule.split('*')[1]))]\n    best=max(matches,key=lambda x:(x[0],x[1]=='Allow'))\n    print(path, best[1],best[2])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff --check; git diff -- site/robots.txt; cat ANSWER.md; python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrules=[]\nfor line in Path('site/robots.txt').read_text().splitlines():\n    if line.startswith(('Allow:', 'Disallow:')):\n        kind, path=line.split(': ',1)\n        rules.append((kind,path))\nfor path in ['/v1/notes','/v1/notes/drip-line-pressure','/v1/notes/drip-line-pressure/reactions','/v1/me','/v1/auth/token','/admin/']:\n    matches=[(len(rule.replace('*','')), kind,rule) for kind,rule in rules if (path.startswith(rule) if '*' not in rule else path.startswith(rule.split('*')[0]) and path.endswith(rule.split('*')[1]))]\n    best=max(matches,key=lambda x:(x[0],x[1]=='Allow'))\n    print(path, best[1],best[2])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/site/robots.txt b/site/robots.txt\nindex c8746c7..5c1cf96 100644\n--- a/site/robots.txt\n+++ b/site/robots.txt\n@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@\n User-agent: *\n Disallow: /v1/\n+Allow: /v1/notes\n+Disallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions\n Disallow: /admin/\n \n Sitemap: https://fieldnotes.example/sitemap.xml\n# Cause and fix\n\nSearch Console's live inspection of `/n/drip-line-pressure` fetched the page successfully (HTTP 200), but its rendered text was **“NOT FOUND — No note lives at this address.”** The site serves the same HTML shell for every note and `site/app.js` fetches the note from `/v1/notes/{slug}` before rendering it. `site/robots.txt` blocked all of `/v1/`, so Google could fetch the shell but could not fetch the content needed to render the note. The failed fetch entered the app's not-found fallback, which was still served as HTTP 200; Search Console therefore classified the page as a soft 404. A normal browser can load the API and display the note, so browser success does not contradict the inspection result.\n\nI updated `site/robots.txt` to allow `/v1/notes` (the public list and individual note reads) while keeping `/v1/` generally blocked. The more specific `/v1/notes/*/reactions` disallow keeps the POST-only reaction route blocked; `/v1/me`, `/v1/auth/token`, and `/admin/` remain blocked by the existing rules. Under Google's most-specific-match rule, the public reads are allowed and those other paths remain disallowed.\n\nThis is a local source change only. After it is deployed, verify the live robots.txt and use Search Console's live URL inspection to check that the rendered page contains the note rather than the fallback. Indexing status may take additional crawls to update.\n/v1/notes Allow /v1/notes\n/v1/notes/drip-line-pressure Allow /v1/notes\n/v1/notes/drip-line-pressure/reactions Disallow /v1/notes/*/reactions\n/v1/me Disallow /v1/\n/v1/auth/token Disallow /v1/\n/admin/ Disallow /admin/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"Search Console fetched the note page with HTTP 200, but rendered the app’s “NOT FOUND” fallback. The page’s content comes from `/v1/notes/{slug}`, which `robots.txt` blocked for crawlers. Browsers could load that API response, so the page appeared normal there.\n\nI updated [robots.txt](/tmp/h-1DxN5U/site/robots.txt) to allow public note reads while keeping the other API routes blocked, and documented the cause and fix in [ANSWER.md](/tmp/h-1DxN5U/ANSWER.md). Local rule checks passed. Nothing was deployed or submitted; the live Search Console result can only be verified after the change is deployed."}}
